  <section class="py-5 bg-white" id="faq">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="text-center mb-5">
        <h2 class="heading-border heading-center mb-3 pb-3 d-inline-block">FAQ</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto">
          <div class="accordion legal-industry-faq" id="legalIndustryFaq">
            <div class="accordion-item border rounded mb-2">
              <h3 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#legfaq1" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="legfaq1">How do you handle AI accuracy in a legal context?</button>
              </h3>
              <div id="legfaq1" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#legalIndustryFaq">
                <div class="accordion-body">We treat every AI output as a draft, never as an authority. Document parsing extracts fields for human review in a split-screen UI. Language refinement preserves the raw observation alongside the refined version. Document generation uses deterministic templates rendered from structured data, not free-form AI output. The audit log records both the AI draft and the human-approved version. A reviewer evaluating the system can trace any record back to its source observation.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="accordion-item border rounded mb-2">
              <h3 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#legfaq2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="legfaq2">How do you ensure tenant isolation in multi-tenant builds?</button>
              </h3>
              <div id="legfaq2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#legalIndustryFaq">
                <div class="accordion-body">PostgreSQL Row Level Security enforced at the database layer. Every table has a tenant_id column. RLS policies use a session-level variable set at authentication time to filter all queries automatically. Even if an application query forgets a tenant filter, or a SQL injection bypasses the application layer, the database refuses to return cross-tenant data. The isolation is structural, not procedural.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="accordion-item border rounded mb-2">
              <h3 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#legfaq3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="legfaq3">Do you offer ongoing maintenance and support?</button>
              </h3>
              <div id="legfaq3" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#legalIndustryFaq">
                <div class="accordion-body">Yes. Most legal-tech clients move to a monthly retainer after the initial build for monitoring, vendor management, feature work, and compliance updates as regulations evolve. We do not take on builds without a clear post-launch support plan.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="accordion-item border rounded mb-2">
              <h3 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#legfaq4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="legfaq4">What if we&rsquo;re already mid-build and need help?</button>
              </h3>
              <div id="legfaq4" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#legalIndustryFaq">
                <div class="accordion-body">We offer a two-week architecture review for teams who have an in-progress legal operations build and need senior eyes on the data flow, AI scoping, and audit defensibility. We audit the existing system, identify risks, and produce a remediation plan you can hand to your team. About a third of these engagements expand into us doing the remediation work; the others get a written plan and run it internally.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
